<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Quarterstaff</h1>
<p>Average Length: Approx. 1.25 times the wielder's height
Type of Weapon: Hand-to-hand.
</p><p>The quarterstaff is the simplest form of the polearm weapon in medieval Europe. It was simply a long wooden pole. Not particularly effective in a fight against an opponent in armor or wielding anything other than a wooden weapon, the quarterstaff was an excellent weapon for travelers as it doubled both as a walking staff and as a deterrent against brigands. The quarterstaff was used more in fencing and brawling than melee combat.
</p><p>These weapons are typically carved by the owner/wielder, and so therefore the size differs from staff to staff. The quarterstaff name is derived from how they are to be wielded: at the middle with the left hand, placing the right halfway between the left hand and the end of the staff.
</p>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="In_Valhalla">In Valhalla</span></h2>
<p>In Valhalla the quarterstaff is a weapon skill of its own, one of the polearms (see <a cmd='#'>Help Weapons</a>): two-handed, it bludgeons, it leans on strength, with some dexterity, and it is of middling speed. It is taught by the fighters from guild level 0, the knights from guild level 0, the paladins from guild level 0, the sorcerers from guild level 0, the druids from guild level 2, the necromancers from guild level 4, the rangers from guild level 5, the conjurers from guild level 8 (up to 90%), the healers from guild level 8 and the assassins from guild level 25. Rangers can also carve one from a fallen branch (see <a cmd='#'>Help Fashion Weapon</a>).
</p><p><br />
